{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f67e39d99b57bc5b64", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Solutions - Test 3", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 37, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232aeb"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329f1", "title": "Chemistry Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232978", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b43"], "question": {"text": "A solution containing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>62</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> ethylene glycol in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> water is cooled to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> . If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math> for water is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.86</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kg</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> , the amount of water (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> ) separated as ice is:"}, "options": [{"id": "69ecc4", "text": "<math><mn>48</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232979"}, {"id": "7e4e7b", "text": "<math><mn>64</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923297a"}, {"id": "5f79d8", "text": "<math><mn>16</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923297b"}, {"id": "2c6e1a", "text": "<math><mn>32</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923297c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923297d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4794"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5658"], "question": {"text": "A solution is made by mixing one mole of volatile liquid \\(A\\) with 3 moles of volatile liquid \\(B\\). The vapour pressure of pure A is 200 mm Hg and that of the solution is 500 mm Hg. The vapour pressure of pure \\(B\\) and the least volatile component of the solution, respectively, are :"}, "options": [{"id": "905c5b", "text": "\\(1400 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}, \\mathrm{A}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923297e"}, {"id": "b6d709", "text": "\\(1400 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}, \\mathrm{B}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923297f"}, {"id": "a24fc2", "text": "\\(600 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}, \\mathrm{B}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232980"}, {"id": "dd41b9", "text": "\\(600 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}, \\mathrm{A}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232981"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232982", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b67"], "question": {"text": "\\(0.05 \\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{CuSO}_4\\) when treated with \\(0.01 \\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{K}_2 \\mathrm{Cr}_2 \\mathrm{O}_7\\) gives green colour solution of \\(\\mathrm{Cu}_2 \\mathrm{Cr}_2 \\mathrm{O}_7\\). The two solutions are separated as shown below :\n[SPM : Semi Permeable Membrane]\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FYSyNWOMZRJP294n49WnPFvCPBleWKj1mM9wUTMD7OYE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br />Due to osmosis :"}, "options": [{"id": "221d8f", "text": "Molarity of \\(\\mathrm{CuSO}_4\\) solution is lowered.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232983"}, {"id": "245837", "text": "Molarity of \\(\\mathrm{K}_2 \\mathrm{Cr}_2 \\mathrm{O}_7\\) solution is lowered.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232984"}, {"id": "5f94f1", "text": "Green colour formation observed on side Y.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232985"}, {"id": "b13cb7", "text": "Green colour formation observed on side X.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232986"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232987", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4794"], "concepts": ["6162fbc16ed13040ec852ae8"], "question": {"text": "Liquids <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> form an ideal solution in the entire composition range. At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>350</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the vapour pressure of pure A and pure B are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>Pa</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>Pa</mi></math> , respectively. The composition of the vapour in equilibrium with a solution containing 40 mole percent of A at this temperature is:"}, "options": [{"id": "8798cd", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo>;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232988"}, {"id": "a68fa2", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.76</mn><mo>;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.24</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232989"}, {"id": "48605b", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.28</mn><mo>;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.72</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923298a"}, {"id": "7498f5", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.37</mn><mo>;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.63</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923298b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923298c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52c8"], "question": {"text": "1.24 g of \\(\\mathrm{AX}_2\\) (molar mass \\(124 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\) ) is dissolved in 1 kg of water to form a solution with boiling point of \\(100.0156^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\), while \\(25.4 \\mathrm{~g}^{\\circ}\\) of \\(\\mathrm{AY}_2\\) (molar mass \\(250 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\) ) in 2 kg of water constitutes a solution with a boiling point of \\(100.0260^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\).\n\\(\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{b}}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\right)=0.52 \\mathrm{~K} \\mathrm{~kg} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\)\nWhich of the following is correct ?"}, "options": [{"id": "22cf7a", "text": "\\(\\mathrm{AX}_2\\) is fully ionised while \\(\\mathrm{AY}_2\\) is completely unionised.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923298d"}, {"id": "5e661e", "text": "\\(\\mathrm{AX}_2\\) is completely unionised while \\(\\mathrm{AY}_2\\) is fully ionised.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923298e"}, {"id": "26a3f2", "text": "\\(\\mathrm{AX}_2\\) and \\(\\mathrm{AY}_2\\) (both) are completely unionised.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923298f"}, {"id": "c2ac9e", "text": "\\(\\mathrm{AX}_2\\) and \\(\\mathrm{AY}_2\\) (both) are fully ionised.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232990"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232991", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["6117b92c67dbe2603c3e949f"], "question": {"text": "<p>We have three aqueous solutions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> labelled as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>‘</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>’</mo><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mo>‘</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>’</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>‘</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>’</mo></math> with concentration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>001</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>,</mo></math> respectively. The value of van <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>’</mo></math> Haft factor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math> for these solutions will be in the order.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "afc71e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232992"}, {"id": "571ed3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232993"}, {"id": "bfbd5e", "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub></math></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232994"}, {"id": "f66ed3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232995"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232996", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c6337"], "question": {"text": "At room temperature, a dilute solution of urea is prepared by dissolving <math><mn>0.60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of urea in <math><mn>360</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of water. If the vapour pressure of pure water at this temperature is <math><mn>35</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> , lowering of vapour pressure will be:<br />(molar mass of urea <math><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> )"}, "options": [{"id": "9e14c5", "text": "<math><mn>0.028</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232997"}, {"id": "599586", "text": "<math><mn>0.027</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232998"}, {"id": "d30174", "text": "<math><mn>0.031</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232999"}, {"id": "ee0fae", "text": "<math><mn>0.017</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923299a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923299b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b43"], "question": {"text": "Two solutions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> are prepared by dissolving <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of non-volatile solutes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>. respectively in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> of water. The ratio of depression in freezing points for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. The ratio of molar masses of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "653962", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923299c"}, {"id": "feb417", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923299d"}, {"id": "d17325", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923299e"}, {"id": "a76846", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923299f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329a0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52c8"], "question": {"text": "2 moles each of ethylene glycol and glucose are dissolved in 500 g of water. The boiling point of the resulting solution is :<br />(Given : Ebullioscopic constant of water $\\left.=0.52 \\mathrm{~K} \\mathrm{~kg} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\right)$"}, "options": [{"id": "05e683", "text": "379.2 K", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329a1"}, {"id": "3dc25a", "text": "377.3 K", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329a2"}, {"id": "dded0a", "text": "375.3 K", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329a3"}, {"id": "f48aae", "text": "277.3 K", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329a4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329a5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b67"], "question": {"text": "A solution is prepared by dissolving 0.6 g of urea (molar mass <math><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) and <math><mn>1.8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of glucose (molar mass <math><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) in 100 mL of water at <math><msup><mrow><mn>27</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The osmotic pressure of the solution is:<br />(<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.08206</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math><math><mtext> atm</mtext></math> <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "8d7178", "text": "<math><mn>8.2</mn></math> atm", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329a6"}, {"id": "2ad054", "text": "<math><mn>2.46</mn></math> atm", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329a7"}, {"id": "18af31", "text": "<math><mn>4.92</mn></math> atm", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329a8"}, {"id": "6f52d9", "text": "<math><mn>1.64</mn></math> atm", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329a9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329aa", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["6117b92c67dbe2603c3e949f"], "question": {"text": "Arrange the following solutions in order of their increasing boiling points.\n(i) $10^{-4} \\mathrm{M~} \\mathrm{NaCl}$\n(ii) $10^{-4} \\mathrm{M~}$ Urea\n(iii) $10^{-3} \\mathrm{M~} \\mathrm{NaCl}$\n(iv) $10^{-2} \\mathrm{M~} \\mathrm{NaCl}$"}, "options": [{"id": "803fe2", "text": "(i)  &lt; (ii) &lt; (iii) &lt; (iv)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329ab"}, {"id": "4809bb", "text": "(iv)  &lt; (iii) &lt; (i) &lt; (ii)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329ac"}, {"id": "5b8202", "text": "(ii)  &lt; (i$) \\equiv($iii) &lt; (iv)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329ad"}, {"id": "daf5cb", "text": "(ii)  &lt; (i) &lt; (iii) &lt; (iv)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329ae"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329af", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b43"], "question": {"text": "Which one of the following <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;aqueous solutions will exhibit the largest freezing point depression?"}, "options": [{"id": "4fb046", "text": "glycine", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329b0"}, {"id": "775400", "text": "hydrazine", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329b1"}, {"id": "732b88", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KHSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329b2"}, {"id": "8b050a", "text": "glucose", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329b3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329b4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52c8"], "question": {"text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of a non-volatile non-electrolyte solute is dissolved in <math><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of two different solvents <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and B whose ebullioscopic constants are in the ratio of <math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. The ratio of the elevation in their boiling points, <math><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math>, is: (assuming they have the same molar mass)"}, "options": [{"id": "698745", "text": "<math><mn>10</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329b5"}, {"id": "193d4a", "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329b6"}, {"id": "51fdc1", "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>0.2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329b7"}, {"id": "7f7f1c", "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329b8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329b9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b67"], "question": {"text": "$X Y$ is the membrane / partition between two chambers 1 and 2 containing sugar solutions of concentration $c_1$ and $c_2\\left(c_1 \\gt c_2\\right) \\mathrm{mol} \\mathrm{L}^{-1}$. For the reverse osmosis to take place identify the correct condition<br />(Here $p_1$ and $p_2$ are pressures applied on chamber 1 and 2)<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F-dNZdN-4rlHmVkUgxMoYKNgMBv45UbU5eMz2VyCl9Ks.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br />(A) Membrane/Partition; Cellophane, $\\mathrm{p}_1 \\gt \\pi$<br />(B) Membrane/Partition ; Porous. $\\mathrm{p}_2 \\gt \\pi$<br />(C) Membrane/Partition ; Parchment paper, $\\mathrm{p}_1 \\gt \\pi$<br />(D) Membrane/Partition : Cellophane, $\\mathrm{p}_2 \\gt \\pi$<br />Choose the correct answer from the option given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "5e285c", "text": "B and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329ba"}, {"id": "119102", "text": "A and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329bb"}, {"id": "a2f366", "text": "A and C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329bc"}, {"id": "819688", "text": "C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329bd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329be", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["6117b92c67dbe2603c3e949f"], "question": {"text": "$\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{HgI}_{4}$ is $40 \\%$ ionised in aqueous solution. The value of its van't Hoff factor (i) is:"}, "options": [{"id": "b5f278", "text": "1.6", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329bf"}, {"id": "d356fc", "text": "1.8", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329c0"}, {"id": "ccda3d", "text": "20", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329c1"}, {"id": "e9eb53", "text": "22", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329c2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329c3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b43"], "question": {"text": "The solution from the following with highest depression in freezing point/lowest freezing point is"}, "options": [{"id": "d2a94e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn></math> g of acetic acid dissolved in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo> </mo></math>of aqueous solution.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329c4"}, {"id": "0672ce", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn></math> g of acetic acid dissolved in benzene", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329c5"}, {"id": "7f335e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn></math> g of benzoic acid dissolved in benzene", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329c6"}, {"id": "778a91", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn></math> g of glucose dissolved in water", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329c7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329c8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52c8"], "question": {"text": "The elevation in boiling point for <math><mn>1</mn></math> molal solution of glucose is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The depression in freezing point for <math><mn>2</mn></math> molal solution of glucose in the same solvent is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2&#160;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The relation between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "3b8538", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329c9"}, {"id": "4dd367", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.5</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329ca"}, {"id": "b3c027", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329cb"}, {"id": "695dd4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.5</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329cc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329cd", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b43"], "question": {"text": "<p>What happens to freezing point of benzene when small quantity of napthalene is added to benzene?  </p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9bc01f", "text": "Increases", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329ce"}, {"id": "51fda9", "text": "Remains unchanged ", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329cf"}, {"id": "00ddb2", "text": "First decreases and then increases", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329d0"}, {"id": "79a2fa", "text": "Decreases", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329d1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329d2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b43"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :\nStatement (I) : NaCl is added to the ice at $0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, present in the ice cream box to prevent the melting of ice cream.\nStatement (II) : On addition of NaCl to ice at $0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, there is a depression in freezing point.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "6355fc", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329d3"}, {"id": "9a204a", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329d4"}, {"id": "3f46d8", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329d5"}, {"id": "553161", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329d6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329d7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b43"], "question": {"text": "Consider the given plots of vapour pressure (VP) vs temperature(T/K). Which amongst the following options is correct graphical representation showing $\\Delta \\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{f}}$, depression in the freezing point of a solvent in a solution?"}, "options": [{"id": "abe17e", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F4-GDVhHoQ8O9aeeYo_KcJ5OKMxgKAMwaYx-bU-eRjRQ.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92329d8"}, {"id": "57216b", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FMR6JSN-SQBYdWga8POFIzrRqmK8Ax4ciUiEcrn2f8V0.original.fullsize.png?alt=me