org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math> Torr and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> Torr, respectively. If the liquid mixture contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;mole fraction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, then the mole fraction of liquid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> in the vapour phase is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>17</mn></mfrac></math>. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&nbsp;is"}, "options": [{"id": "e2467f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232acd"}, {"id": "089cf7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ace"}, {"id": "bc1f9b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232acf"}, {"id": "244112", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ad0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ad1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c6337"], "question": {"text": "\\(2.5 \\mathrm{~g}\\) of a non-volatile, non-electrolyte is dissolved in \\(100 \\mathrm{~g}\\) of water at \\(25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\). The solution showed a boiling point elevation by \\(2^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\). Assuming the solute concentration is negligible with respect to the solvent concentration, the vapor pressure of the resulting aqueous solution is \\(\\qquad\\) \\(\\mathrm{mm}\\) of \\(\\mathrm{Hg}\\) (nearest integer)\n[Given : Molal boiling point elevation constant of water \\(\\left(\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{b}}\\right)=0.52 \\mathrm{~K} . \\mathrm{kg} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\\),\n\\(1 \\mathrm{~atm}\\) pressure \\(=760 \\mathrm{~mm}\\) of \\(\\mathrm{Hg}\\), molar mass of water \\(=18 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\)]"}, "options": [{"id": "ff22d5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ad2"}, {"id": "ee7483", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ad3"}, {"id": "03434f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ad4"}, {"id": "2e96f9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ad5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ad6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["6117b60b478ae845c43c6434"], "concepts": ["6117b608478ae845c43c6352"], "question": {"text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> gas is bubbled through water at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>303</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, the number of millimoles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> gas that dissolve in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> litre of water is____(Nearest integer) (Given : Henry&#39;s Law constant for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>303</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>46</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>82</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> bar and partial pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>920</mn></math> bar)<br />(Assume solubility of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> in water is too small, nearly negligible)"}, "options": [{"id": "16af58", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ad7"}, {"id": "6fff63", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ad8"}, {"id": "9138e4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ad9"}, {"id": "0798c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ada"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232adb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df97"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b79"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b67"], "question": {"text": "The osmotic pressure ($\\pi$) of solutions of PVC in cyclohexanone at 300 K is measured. When a graph of $\\frac{\\pi}{C}$ versus concentration $C$ (in g/L) is plotted, it yields a straight line with a y-intercept of 0.0006 atm L/g. The molar mass of PVC is ______ g/mol (Nearest integer).<br>(Given: R = 0.083 L atm K⁻¹ mol⁻¹)"}, "options": [{"id": "904bb1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232adc"}, {"id": "d79eac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232add"}, {"id": "c5b5ab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232ade"}, {"id": "48e07f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232adf"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:33.591Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:33.591Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9232aea"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:16:06.704Z", "upd